## Context

The observatory is an independent public research output: country portfolios and project descriptions with sources, timelines, totals and useful visual exploration. Its usefulness must not depend on demonstrating acceleration.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First browser acceptance test on a small release fixture: navigate country → filtered project → milestone source, and country total → constituent records. Include missing dates, a disputed amount and overlapping components; these must be legible and must not appear as zero progress or duplicate financing.

## Actions

Choose the simplest maintainable site approach after inspecting existing publishing infrastructure. Build accessible country and project pages, filters, portfolio/stage visualisations, timelines, source links and downloadable release access. Display last-reviewed and release dates. Produce a concrete preview, hosting proposal and public URL decision before launch; publish the reviewed site and verify the live route. Do not require interactive complexity where a clear table suffices.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Four country pages and stable project URLs expose essential features and evidence
- [ ] Totals and filters reconcile exactly with the selected dataset edition
- [ ] Timelines separate dated events from status-only observations and missing data
- [ ] Readable mobile/desktop and keyboard navigation; meaningful visualisations
- [ ] Preview reviewed, hosting/URL resolved and public site verified with release metadata

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

## Storage implementation contract

Build from Markdown dossiers plus frozen CSV/JSON. Initial hosting is static; no live SQLite service and no browser access to DVC. Reuse generated registry features and timelines rather than duplicating facts in Markdown. Test a render without network or DVC from the frozen package.

## GitHub planning issue

https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/climate-finance-het/issues/1335

## Progress audit, 14 September 2026

The local static MVP exists in PR #1343 and exercises country synthesis, project
pages, filters, source links, downloads and historical browsing. This does not
close the public-site ticket. After the scientific fixes and 0726 release checks,
review keyboard navigation, stable deep links, edition metadata and reconciliation
of displayed aggregates. Resolve hosting/public URL using the concrete preview,
then verify the deployed route. The 97 closed World Bank operations remain a
labelled descriptive reference pool; analytical cohort work belongs to 0730.

Check export size as the portfolio grows: the corrected ZAF JSON is approximately
508 KB, close to the repository's 512,000-byte file cap. Before expanding it,
measure payload/load costs and split country/project handoffs if needed while
preserving offline downloads and complete provenance. This is not a reason to
introduce a live database.

## Independent checkpoint review follow-ups

Before monthly refreshes, add regression fixtures for a project with both a year
interval and a later point event, and for an unreviewed timing row carrying
bounds. Define interval-aware display order and reject unsupported established
bounds without converting reviewed intervals into invented point dates. Current
451 timing rows contain neither problematic combination; these are refresh
hardening tasks identified by the PR #1343 correctness review.

Derive undisclosed counts in all views from the exported overview; the current
three hardcoded mentions agree at 21 but create future refresh drift. First test:
change the fixture's undisclosed count and require all three views to follow it.
